1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,440
Then they move on to the relationship with the self

2
00:00:04,720 --> 00:00:06,680
And we begin talking about the relationship with the self

3
00:00:06,840 --> 00:00:08,240
We'll say the following

4
00:00:08,400 --> 00:00:13,080
That the relationship with the self is built upon purification

5
00:00:13,360 --> 00:00:16,200
Purification as the basis? Yes

6
00:00:17,360 --> 00:00:18,920
Not upon entertainment

7
00:00:19,560 --> 00:00:20,920
Nor upon finding gratitude

8
00:00:21,160 --> 00:00:22,720
Nor upon development

9
00:00:22,960 --> 00:00:24,720
Nor upon glorification

10
00:00:25,640 --> 00:00:27,800
No, it's built upon purification

11
00:00:28,200 --> 00:00:32,720
The Muslim scholars interested in behaviors

12
00:00:34,120 --> 00:00:37,680
Confirm that the first gate towards purification

13
00:00:37,680 --> 00:00:41,160
Is when a person thinks ill of himself

14
00:00:41,320 --> 00:00:42,960
When a person thinks ill of himself...

15
00:00:43,080 --> 00:00:45,680
And thinks well of his Lord and of others.

16
00:00:47,960 --> 00:00:52,920
As if a person thought well of himself

17
00:00:53,040 --> 00:00:56,760
He will grow arrogant and haughty, and become full of himself

18
00:00:57,440 --> 00:01:00,160
And will negatively be satisfied with himself, and will not seek to improve it
